id: pm-odw3j8
title: Return an expected SDK refusal for impossible relationship context budgets
description: "Sentry PM-CLI-3N reports four handled production CLI TypeErrors in published2026.10.19: Relationship context tokenBudget cannot fit root and evidence, classified unclassified_runtime_error with exit1. The SDK command's controlled initial budget-floor signal should become an expected usage refusal with actionable budget and bounded-inspection guidance. Preserve low-level graph primitive TypeErrors, successful context packing, internal rendered-budget floor behavior and genuine runtime error reporting."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: bug,cli,observability,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-19T16:07:50.190Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T16:54:35.792Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#2b1352b8d1f9ffd894ba9de2"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce the published budget-floor classification with a failing-before sandbox control; Translate only the existing controlled initial budget-floor signal into the public expected-error shape and usage exit2; Preserve low-level primitive errors and successful/shrinking packet behavior; Execute returned compact inspection guidance and verify SDK CLI and MCP refusal parity; Resolve the verified Sentry issue with release-aware evidence without deleting history or weakening observability gates
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "Relationship packets stay within their selected rendered JSON/TOON budget including aliases and lean projection, or return an expected usage refusal with executable compact recovery; CLI and MCP preserve the error while primitive TypeErrors and fatal faults remain unchanged."
